<title>FINLAND: Finnair Jan load factor up at 66.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Finnair Jan load factor up at 66.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish national airline Finnair Oy said in a statement on Friday its passenger load factor rose 3.1 percentage points year-on-year in January to 66.3 percent.  </p>
<p>Finnair gave the following statistics:</p>
<p>					Jan 1997    Dec 1996   Yr/yr(pct)</p>
<p> Passengers (thousand)	     478	   474	  +8.7</p>
<p> RPK (million)			 917	   922	  +9.2</p>
<p> RTK (million)			 105	   109	 +11.5</p>
<p> Cargo and mail (thousand kg)  5,554	 6,481	 +15.4</p>
<p> Passenger load factor (pct)    66.3	  69.8	  +3.1 pts</p>
<p>January 1997 totals broken down by flight type:</p>
<p>			Passengers   RPK	 RTK	    Cargo</p>
<p>			thousand   million    million     thousand kg</p>
<p> International	 256	 683	  84	    4,980</p>
<p> Domestic		188	  84	   7		494</p>
<p> Charter		  35	 150	  14		 80</p>
<p>Load factor (percent) by flight type:</p>
<p>				  Jan 1997   Dec 1996   Yr/yr (pct pts)</p>
<p> International		  65.5	 68.8	  +3.4</p>
<p> Domestic			 50.0	 56.7	  +1.2</p>
<p>Finnair's financial year runs from April 1 to March 31.</p>
<p>RPK - revenue passenger km (revenue passengers carried multiplied by km flown)</p>
<p>RTK - revenue tonne km (tonnage of revenue load carried -- passengers, cargo and mail -- multiplied by km flown.</p>
<p>Passenger load factor - RPK as a percentage of available seat km</p>
<p>Finnair does not give a cargo load factor.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358 - 9 - 680 50 235</p>
</text>
